# Git Commit Rules

## Commit message format
Use conventional commits — always:

```
<type>: <short description in lowercase>
```

| Type | When to use |
|------|-------------|
| `feat` | New feature or user-facing capability |
| `fix` | Bug fix |
| `chore` | Maintenance, deps, config (no production code change) |
| `refactor` | Code restructuring with no behavior change |
| `style` | UI-only changes (layout, spacing, colors) |
| `perf` | Performance improvement |
| `docs` | Documentation only |
| `test` | Adding or fixing tests |

Examples:
```
feat: add saved search alert emails
fix: restore listing hero photo on mobile
style: tighten broker card spacing on team page
chore: update supabase-js to 2.98.0
```

## Workflow
1. Make changes on a branch from current `origin/main`.
2. `git add -A` (or stage intentionally — never commit secrets)
3. `git commit -m "type: description"`
4. **Push that branch to GitHub in the same session** with `npm run push`. All code work is pushed to GitHub as a branch right away. Do not leave finished work only on a local branch. Matt uses Claude Code and Cursor interchangeably; unpushed commits are invisible to the other tool and are not “shipped.”
5. A finished unit is `npm run ship`. Unfinished work stays `npm run push`. Never `git push` `main`. No rebase, force-push, or reset. If the pull request conflicts with `main`, stop.

Pre-commit runs `npm test`. Pre-push runs the full quality gate.

## Bypass hooks (sparingly)
```bash
SKIP_LOCAL_GATES=1 git push      # skip all quality gates
SKIP_DB_GUARD=1 git push         # skip migration drift check only
```

## Branch strategy
- **Production is `main`.** A finished unit is `npm run ship`. Never `git push` `main`. Vercel deploys `main` (a docs-only diff may skip via `ignoreCommand`).
- **Worktrees allowed** for parallel agents / experiments — name `wt/<topic>-YYYYMMDD`, push the branch right away, or record it in `CROSS_AGENT_HANDOFF.md` before stopping. See `.cursor/rules/always-merge-to-main.mdc` and **AGENTS.md → Worktrees**.
- Push the branch to GitHub right away. Do not keep the only copy local.
- A finished unit is `npm run ship`. Never `git push` `main`.
- No rebase, force-push, or reset.

## Do NOT
- Commit `.env.local` or any file containing secrets
- Force-push
- Rebase or reset
- Leave valued work only on an unpushed worktree with no handoff entry
- Leave the working tree dirty before switching tasks — always commit or stash
